* Datasheet checked against: DS11108 Rev. 28-2, vendor/bjt_npn/diodes_inc/BC847B/BC846A-BC848C_DS11108.pdf.
* Instantiate: Qxxx C B E DI_BC847A    (pin order collector, base, emitter; no substrate node)
* Model name: DI_BC847A   (NOT BC847A: the vendor's .MODEL carries the DI_ prefix)
*
* Verdict against the datasheet (scripts/validate_models.py, set temp = 25):
*   hFE 210.2 at IC = 2 mA, VCE = 5 V against 110..220 (typ 180): INSIDE, 4.5% under the ceiling. VBE(on) 678.5 mV against 580..700 (typ 660): inside. Capacitances and fT are not locked on the A grade (hFE only); see bc847b.lib.
* Not modelled / to know: no KF/AF (no 1/f noise); XTI is not given and takes
* ngspice's default 3; the model has no DATE or VERSION line. Vendor disclaimer
* (AS IS, no warranty) follows unaltered in the vendor block below.
*
* ONE CHANGE TO THE VENDOR TEXT, declared in the .provenance.json: the vendor
* file has a bare line 'BJTs' (a comment wrapped without its '*') which ngspice
* 47 reads as a B source and dies on ('mal formed B source instance: bjts',
* exit 1). It is turned into '*BJTs'. Nothing else differs.
*
